# Quality gates

Run these before claiming a task is done. Failures must be fixed, not bypassed.

## Full repo

```bash
npm run typecheck      # tsc --noEmit (strict, no implicit any)
npm run lint           # ESLint strict + no-explicit-any error
npm run check:lint     # alias for full-repo ESLint
npm run test:unit      # Vitest
npx knip               # dead code / unused exports
```

## Module-scoped (fast, dark-factory verify)

```bash
node scripts/fabro-verify.mjs
```

Module-scoped `tsc` + ESLint (ignores errors outside the target module), module unit
tests, **then husky pre-commit parity**: `check-architecture.mjs`, `check-docs-updated.mjs
--working-tree`, full `npm run test:unit`, `npm run build`. Passing fabro-verify means
**git commit pre-commit hooks would pass** after staging. Reads module from `PLAN.md`.
Uses `NODE_OPTIONS=--max-old-space-size=6144`.

## E2E

```bash
npm run test:e2e                # Playwright default
npm run test:e2e smoke          # storyteller smoke script
npm run test:e2e full-loop      # full storyteller loop
```

## Baseline / ratchets

Typecheck and ESLint warnings are ratcheted — never increase the baseline count. See `docs/quality-improvement-spec.md`. `.local/` is for ad-hoc tooling (gitignored); don't add throwaway plumbing under `src/lib`.

## Order of operations (mirror Fabro build path)

1. Implement (use skills: `/refactor`, `/write-tests`, `/review`).
2. `node scripts/fabro-verify.mjs` → fix → repeat (max 3 fix loops; includes pre-commit parity).
3. Retro (evidence-based — `git diff` verified).

Optional locally after fabro-verify pass: `npx knip`, `npm run test:e2e full-loop` (storyteller UI).
